# Location screens (tabletop board + 3D pieces)

Marc locked this (Oct 2026). **Every location screen** — the Lythmere map and Inn, Market, Club, Riverside (and any future place) — is a **flat painted board with separate 3D models sitting on it**. Canonical look-test: `mockups/lythmere-hex-pieces/`.

Never generate the board and the pieces as one picture. That always reads as a drawing.

Live `index.html` still uses street paintings + oak standees. Leave that until a rebuild is asked. **New** location work uses this language only. Do not generate isometric overworlds, walkable streets, or display-style pages.

## Two layers

1. **Board** — one 720×1280 (`9:16`) painting. Flat. No buildings, no people, no HUD, no town name, no hex grid. Aged sepia / olive / ochre, candlelit, vignetted. Slight look-down at a board, not a 3D valley model.
2. **Pieces** — each landmark generated **alone**, 1:1, on lime `#00FF00`. Three-quarter, **~35° above the table**, one warm light from the **upper left**, chunky **hex base** with a visible earth side wall. Same muted palette. No people, no letters. Key with `mockups/lythmere-hex-pieces/key_pieces.py`, trim, ~520px wide, under ~500KB.

Composite in HTML. Contact shadow on each piece. Marc places in **% of the board** (`x` / `y` = base centre, `w` ≈ 34–36%, `anchor` ≈ 62–72%). Lower on the board = in front. Labels are HTML.

Full recipe: `mockups/lythmere-hex-pieces/README.md`.

## HUD (every location screen)

Overlay, never paint.

- Date + Journal paper plaques at the top (`paper_corner.png` / `paper_seal.png`).
- Place name is HTML in the gap **under** those plaques (not baked into the jpg).
- **No** bottom place-name strip on these screens. The pieces are the navigation.
- Safe-area: `max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-*) + 10px)`.
- Stage: **390px × 9:16** on a laptop; on a phone `100dvh` / `100svh`. Not a leftover-space match-table scaler.

## What sits on a location

- **Overworld (Lythmere map):** Inn, Market, Club, Riverside as hex-base terrain. **No NPCs** on this map — they are at a location.
- **Inside a location:** same two layers, closer shot of that place’s floor/mat. Furniture and stalls are pieces. People are **separate keyed figures**, not painted into the board.
- People construction stays Tomas oak bevel until Marc picks otherwise. Do not invent isometric walkers or put people on hex bases.

## Do

- Repeat this recipe for every new location screen.
- Let Marc drag pieces (same placer pattern as `mockups/lythmere-hex-pieces/index.html`). Do not eyeball new towns.
- Keep match / binder / journal / claim as leftover-space gilt screens.

## Do not

- Ask a generator for “flat map with 3D things on it” in one shot
- Paint HUD, titles, hex grid, or people into the board
- Generate a new isometric town or street you walk
- Put NPCs on the overworld map
- Use Mark spots for a new location
- Split `index.html` just to start this rebuild — say so first
- Change Baseline V1, Claim One, or calendar to make the map work
